PRODUCT (read carefully)
- "AI-стол": a D&D-style game for ONE room. A big touch screen lies flat on the table; 4 players sit two per long side (the far side's UI is rotated 180°). A TV shows the shared scene. Phones can play too. The host has an operator console (/admin). A live AI game master "Северин Кроу" talks and listens (push-to-talk voice, Russian). Players roll REAL physical dice and type/say the result; the server rolls enemy dice openly. Rule: nothing changes in the world until someone confirms the proposed action («Подтвердить»). One campaign («Чёрная вода у Мельничьего Брода», slavic-fairy-tale dark fantasy), heroes: Никита Кожемяка, Настасья Микулична, Лиса Патрикеевна, Старец Подорожник, Кощей, Любава. Phases: setup (pick party) → story beats with choices → encounter (lay out fight) → turn-based fight on a grid map (abilities, targets, dice) → rest → ending.
- Current code: /home/kesha/projects/ai-table-mvp on the VPS (reach it ONLY via `ssh orchestra-vps '<cmd>'`, read-only). Web: web/table.html, scene.html, admin.html, start.html, web/src/shared/*.ts (client.ts, tabletop.ts, combat.ts, fx.ts, art.ts, voice.ts, sound.ts), web/src/shared/shell.css, theme.css.
- Current screenshots (local PNG, open with the Read tool): claude-code-game-master/build/ai-table-gallery/img/ — e.g. 03-setup-tabletop.png, 23-fight-table.png, 25-fight-tabletop.png, 24-fight-phone.png, 26-fight-scene.png, 27-fight-admin.png, 21-moment-roll-card-table.png, 15-encounter-table.png, 09-story-table.png, 38-ending-scene.png. Captions with observed problems: claude-code-game-master/build/ai-table-gallery/captions.json.
- Owner's concept art (the visual target he liked): claude-code-game-master/build/ai-table-gallery/img/concept/ (choose-master-severin.jpg, choose-hero-six.jpg, arden-veil-card.jpg, generated_1792048145393.png).

THE OWNER'S VERDICT (2026-11-02, verbatim): «да там пиздец нейрослопный интерфейс говно полностью переделывать как крутая игра сука минимум сука текста и ui и панелей все каеф интерактивное и икокни и значки и то и се крч супер игра супер скиллы … я должен открыть экран и сразу понять что и как делать».
So the goal: a real game look and feel — minimal text, minimal panels, icon-first, interactive, juicy; open the screen and instantly know what to do. Today it is dark panels full of small text, default checkboxes/selects, service labels, huge empty areas, tiny map.

HARD CONSTRAINTS that a redesign must keep: physical dice entered by players (never altered); confirm-before-change; 4 seats 2+2 on the flat table with the far side rotated; no scrolling anywhere; Russian UI; TV readable from a sofa; phone playable; voice push-to-talk to the GM; every existing function must stay reachable (can be hidden/merged).

RULES FOR YOU: read-only everywhere (no edits on the VPS or hub, no service restarts); never print secret values; cite every claim (URL, or file path / command). Return structured output only. Write findings in Russian except names, URLs and code identifiers.


You are the lead game-UI designer. 8 researchers (vps, touch-table, companion, hud, onboarding, visual, functions, assets) returned the findings below. Open 4-6 of the current screenshots and the owner's concept images yourself (Read tool) before writing.

Write ONE design brief in Russian Markdown for a before/after CONCEPT of the redesigned table (the concept comes first; implementation later). It must be concrete enough that a designer can build HTML mockups from it without asking questions:
1. "Северная звезда": one paragraph — what playing should feel like; the 3 references we borrow most from and what exactly.
2. 10-14 design rules with numbers (max visible words per state, min text/icon sizes for a flat table at ~60-80 cm and a TV at 3 m, one primary action per state, how the far side is handled, colour coding per hero/side, motion/feedback budget).
3. Visual language: palette (hex), fonts (free, with Cyrillic, licence named), frames/materials, icon style; how it relates to the owner's concept art.
4. Per surface — Большой стол (tabletop, the main one), Телефон, ТВ (scene), Пульт (admin), Вход/Старт — and per phase (подготовка/выбор героев, история с выбором, перед боем, бой: мой ход / ход врага / бросок кубиков / подтверждение, привал, финал): what is on screen (layout sketch in words, with positions), the ONE primary action and how it is signalled, what text remains (exact Russian words, as few as possible), what moved to icons, what is hidden and where.
5. Function map: every current function (from the inventory) → where it lives in the new design (none may be lost).
6. Icon set needed (list with meaning) and which art to reuse from the store vs new images to generate (Codex image generation): exact list with a one-line prompt idea each.
7. The "5-second test": for each main screen, what a newcomer must understand in 5 seconds and how the design guarantees it.
8. What the before/after concept site should show (which screens and moments, side by side) and how it should be built (interactive HTML prototype with real assets is preferred over static pictures; say what is interactive).
9. Risks and open questions for the owner (only real decisions).
Cite sources inline briefly (URL or file). Return the brief text only.

